    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the business-day rule in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` so the registration date now also rolls forward over public holidays.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n- Added a `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` set with the five pinned dates: `2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`.\n- Rewrote `toBusinessDay(...)` to advance one day at a time while the date is a Saturday, Sunday, **or** a listed public holiday, returning the first non-holiday weekday. The day-by-day loop correctly handles chains (e.g. a holiday immediately followed by a weekend, or the consecutive 12-25 \u2192 weekend \u2192 12-28 stretch), matching the reference roll in `AcceptanceBase.toBusinessDay`.\n- Updated the surrounding javadoc so it accurately describes the holiday behavior rather than the old \"weekend \u2192 next Monday\" rule.\n\nBecause this adjusted date is the single value stored as `registrationDate`, everything derived from it (membership-number year segment, daily create limit, bulk-signup warning) automatically computes against the holiday-adjusted date.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
